      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Great idea. I hate how the 'deny; no reply' system ghosts somebody you willingly added on your friend list which has led to arguments between friends in the past (or bothering them for confirmation via Discord).\nYou wouldn't be able to tell if the user is AFK or if they're not replying to the invite request. It would be cool to get clearance if your invite request has expired on their end (disappears after 15 minutes) with an automatic response back to you saying that they might be AFK. They could also be have Streamer mode enabled, and you wouldn't be able to tell either.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-05T04:49:30.752Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be nice if the game tells you if someone denies a join request instead of everyone requiring to deny with a message to let the other person know. That way, they wont end up waiting an eon before giving up and finding something else to do. This can also be used for when the game takes longer than usual to send the request, so the sender can know if it's a game issue, or something on the receiver's end.",
